## Why This Is Asked

Tests distributed-systems thinking: exactly-once, dedup, backpressure, observability.

## Key Concepts

- Exactly-once processing
- Deduplication with dedup_id
- Backpressure strategies (batching, pause vs drop)
- Observability (tracing, metrics, logs)
- Kafka vs Kinesis trade-offs
- Idempotent sinks and compensating actions

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode for idempotent sink write
function writeEvent(evt, sink, store) {
  const id = evt.dedup_id;
  if (store.seen(id)) return;
  sink.write(evt);
  store.markSeen(id);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test guarantees for partial failures?
- How would you ensure exactly-once with at-least-once queues?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to diagnose multi-tenant routing issues with Istio, header propagation, and fast rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Istio routing: VirtualService, DestinationRule, mTLS
- Per-tenant headers, header-based routing
- Redis ACLs and per-tenant keys
- Canary rollouts and latency budgets

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: per-tenant routing rule sketch (illustrative)
const vs = {
  http: [{
    match: [{ headers: { 'x-tenant-id': { exact: 'tenantA' } } }],
    route: [{ destination: { host: 'api-tenantA' } }]
  }]
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you automate rollback with metrics thresholds?
- How would you extend to support dynamic tenant onboarding without restarts?
